# shell: desktop
# PVL-046/PVL-062: rows a change only MOVED are moved, not drawn again.  A
# file arriving in the middle of a listing used to repaint every row under
# it; the rows below an insertion differ from the frame before only in
# where they sit, which is a blit.
wait 8
expect-rows 4
note the selected row is the instrument: its band is ink no redraw can
note invent, so where the band ends up says whether the pixels moved
click-row 1
wait 8
expect-pixel 200 140 336698
draw-reset
note a file arrives that sorts above the selected row
write /tmp/trk_script/0a.txt x
wait 40
expect-rows 5
note the row that appeared is painted, and painted twice more as it
note learns its picture and its size -- three paints for a five-row
note listing, where the frame used to paint every row
expect-drawn 3
note and the rows under it DID move -- the band is a row further down
expect-pixel 200 160 336698
note while the row that appeared is painted where the band used to be
expect-pixel 200 140 ffffff
note the same going the other way: a row goes and the rest closes up over
note it, again without painting the rows that only moved
draw-reset
remove /tmp/trk_script/0a.txt
wait 40
expect-rows 4
expect-drawn 0
expect-pixel 200 140 336698
note and the whole frame, not the pixels a test thought to look at: what
note these frames painted is what a full redraw would have drawn
expect-same-as-redraw
quit
